# Copy to `.dockerignore` at the repo root.
#
# This is a SEPARATE list from .gitignore and people update only one. The consequence of
# the gap is real: `COPY . .` with a stray .env ships production credentials inside the
# image, and deleting it in a later layer does NOT remove it from the image.

node_modules
dist
coverage

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.gitignore

*.test.ts
*.spec.ts
__tests__

Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
.dockerignore

README.md
docs
*.md

.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
